    "body": "Facts from the review fix of PR #2918 (#2789). These are code readings at the pinned solidcore rev `2016386`. They are not runs.\n\n- The parser maps 36 ISO 10303-21 short names to long names at parse time (`SHORT_NAMES`, `solidcore-record/src/step/p21.rs:614-659`; applied at `p21.rs:599`). For the unit entities, the table has `LNGUNT`, `NMDUNT`, `CNBSUN`, `LMWU`, `PAMWU`, `DMNEXP`, `UMWU` and `GMRPCN`.\n- The table does not have a short form of `GLOBAL_UNIT_ASSIGNED_CONTEXT` or `SI_UNIT`. No public source in the repository or in the solidcore checkout states these two short names. PR #2918 does not guess them.\n- The kernel's `length_units` (`crates/kernel/src/solidcore_step.rs:245-289`) finds a context only by the long name `GLOBAL_UNIT_ASSIGNED_CONTEXT`. Otherwise it continues and gives no refusal. An empty list gives no note (the note at lines 195-199 is only for more than one unit).\n- solidcore's `topology.rs:291` reads each solid with `unwrap_or_default()`, which is 1 mm per unit (`units.rs:37-41`).\n- The defect is older than #2904, so it is not a regression. At v0.24.0 the model import used `step_units::mm_per_unit` on ruststep records. ruststep mapped no short names. A short `GLOBAL_UNIT_ASSIGNED_CONTEXT` or a short `LNGUNT` gave `None` there too, and the model was read at 1 mm per unit.\n- The rule that PR #2918 uses for the tool-body read is in `crates/geometry/src/step_units.rs` (`unstated_length_unit`). When no context states a length unit, the read is refused by name if the file has one of these:\n  - a `LENGTH_UNIT`;\n  - an `SI_UNIT` of the metre;\n  - a `CONVERSION_BASED_UNIT` over a `LENGTH_MEASURE_WITH_UNIT`.\n  A file with no unit record keeps 1 mm per unit, as before. The model import can use the same rule.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
